<title>USA: Clinton to make statement after budget talks.</title>
<headline>Clinton to make statement after budget talks.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>President Bill Clinton will make a statement at 4 p.m. EST (2100 GMT) on Wednesday after talks on balancing the budget with the leaders of congressional budget committees, the White House announced.</p>
<p>Clinton will make the statement to a small group of reporters, the White House said. Officials said he would also discuss his trip to Helsinki for a meeting with Russian President Boris Yeltsin. He was to leave for that trip later Wednesday.</p>
</text>
